  "final_text": "**Disposition:** ESCALATE (proposed, awaiting a human decision). Confidence: 0.70.\n\n**Three facts that drove it:**\n1. The trader placed one SELL limit of 31,395, which is 12.9x average top-5 depth. It sat 3 ticks from the touch and had no fills. The trader bought 1,053 on the other side with a market order about 2.8 s later. The SELL was cancelled 158 ms after that.\n2. The price moved 0.5 ticks in the trader's favour. It then reverted 2.5 ticks after the cancel. Cancels were one-sided (cancel_symmetry 0.0).\n3. No legitimate explanation holds. The trader is a registered market maker on SYN.B only, not SYN.A. There was no market event, no risk event and no parent order.\n\n**What would change my mind:** Evidence that the SELL was a genuine client or parent order. The same would apply if the 0.5-tick move came from the trader's own market-order sweep in a thin book and not from the resting SELL. Repeat cycles in a longer time frame would move this toward DRAFT_STOR. I didn't propose DRAFT_STOR because this was a single cycle with a small favourable move.",
